    {
      "type": "updated",
      "source": "wgmods",
      "sourceId": "7661",
      "title": "SpotMeter",
      "previous": {
        "modVersion": "7.0.0",
        "wotGameVersion": "2.3.1.0",
        "fileName": "spotmeter-v7.0.0.wotmod",
        "updatedAt": "2026-07-15T23:25:52.320Z",
        "changeLog": "v7.0.0 - for WoT 2.3.1.0.\n\nMajor update: the in-battle panel is rebuilt on Gameface.\n\nCHANGED\n- The panel is now a Gameface overlay instead of a Scaleform/GUIFlash SWF. SpotMeter ships NO SWF anymore, so it can never collide with another GUIFlash mod's saved window positions. The minimap circle and the whole spot-distance engine are unchanged.\n\nNEW\n- Requires net.openwg.gameface (free, in common modpacks). Without it the circle + hotkeys still work.\n- Modern look: transparent panel, white text, green for the enabled options.\n- Drag the panel by its header (position saved).\n- Collapse arrow: shrink it to just the picked vehicle + spot distance (state remembered).\n\nCleaner log: benign status lines are INFO now (no more warning-looking noise)."
      },
      "current": {
        "modVersion": "7.1.0",
        "wotGameVersion": "2.3.1.1",
        "fileName": "spotmeter-v7.1.0_8glRvc7.wotmod",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-06T21:44:57.316Z",
        "changeLog": "NEW\n- Hover tooltips in the settings menu: every option in the in-garage configurator (a mods-settings menu such as aslainMenu / ModsSettingsAPI) now shows a short hint on hover, in English and Polish - what the option assumes, the exact view-range % for the enemy-loadout toggles and optics/vents/CVS levels, and a note that XVM controls the minimap circle's colour while its minimap is active.\nCHANGED\n- Rebuilt for WoT 2.3.1.1 (minor patch; no other gameplay changes).\nReminder (unchanged since v7.0.0): the in-battle panel is a Gameface overlay and REQUIRES net.openwg.gameface (free, MIT; already in common modpacks). The minimap circle and the hotkeys work even without it."
      }
    },
